  "notes": "Source: Albizu University Miami Campus Catalog (UPDATED February 28, 2026, official PDF), 'Bachelor of Arts in Elementary Education (On-Campus or Online)' PROGRAM BREAKDOWN BY COURSE, hand-transcribed 2026-09-30 from the official PDF. Semester sequence is the collector's ordering (foundations first); the catalog does not print a term-by-term plan — advisor should confirm. Minimum 30 credits must be completed at the Miami Campus. 124 credits: Foundation (39 cr) + Professional Education (24 cr) + Specialization (49 cr) + ESOL Endorsement (12 cr). Prepares for Florida K-6 certification; 2.50 GPA in the major required. Catalog quirks: (1) Several foundation courses are printed with titles only and no course codes (Oral Communication, Behavioral/Life-Physical Sciences, Humanities, Literature, Liberal Arts Elective); shown with descriptive placeholder codes. (2) 'EDE30 Literature and Instructional Tools' appears truncated in the catalog; shown as EDE301X. (3) FLE305 (Cross Cultural Communication) counts in Foundation toward the 15 credits required for the ESOL endorsement. EDE450 student-teaching internship (10 cr) is sequenced last; prerequisite courses may be taken conjointly at the program director's discretion except EDE450.",
